cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  paper it accompanies.
title: >-
  Device-error multiple imputation and Rubin pooling for longitudinal
  actigraphy
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a non-parametric multiple-imputation procedure
  that propagates the measurement difference between two actigraphy systems
  into every estimate of a longitudinal mixed model. Device differences are
  resampled from the empirical distribution of paired concurrent-wear
  differences, the model is refitted once per imputation, and results are
  combined by Rubin's rules so that the instrument uncertainty is carried
  through into all standard errors and confidence intervals. Includes the
  206 paired concurrent-wear differences (22 volunteers, Philips Actiwatch
  versus Axivity AX3) that the published analysis resamples from, released
  under CC BY 4.0.
type: software
license: MIT
